# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TASK 36 B2 — NOTHING IN HERE IS A WEB DOCUMENT.
#
# This is the application root. The only directory a web server should ever
# publish is public/, and the deployment is meant to point its document root
# there. This file is what happens when it does not.
#
# FOUND BY EXECUTION, NOT BY READING. The project sits inside XAMPP's htdocs
# on the development machine, so the project root is also a URL path, and it
# answered:
#
#   GET /photographer/.env                     200   1,360 bytes
#   GET /photographer/.git/config              200     320 bytes
#   GET /photographer/storage/logs/laravel.log 200   7.0 MB
#   GET /photographer/composer.json            200   3,122 bytes
#
# The .env that was being served holds APP_KEY, DB_PASSWORD, MAIL_PASSWORD,
# the AWS pair and PEXELS_API_KEY. The readable .git means the full source and
# the full history, not just one file. There is no application code involved
# in any of it: Apache reads those bytes off the disk and PHP never runs, so
# no middleware, no route and no test inside Laravel could have seen it.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DOES. It denies everything, for every file, at every depth
# below this directory — including storage/, vendor/, .git/, bootstrap/cache/
# and every dotfile. public/.htaccess grants access back for itself, which is
# the one directory that is supposed to be reachable, so a document root
# pointed at either place behaves correctly.
#
# A SERVER THAT IGNORES .htaccess IGNORES THIS, which is why it is a second
# line and not the first. The first line is the document root, and deployment
# must point it at public/. See docs/operations/deployment.md.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Apache 2.4
<IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
    Require all denied
</IfModule>

# Apache 2.2 and earlier
<IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
    Order allow,deny
    Deny from all
</IfModule>

# Belt and braces for a server that honours mod_rewrite but not the above.
<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
    RewriteEngine On
    RewriteRule ^ - [F,L]
</IfModule>
